<h3>1.4 Language use, impossibility claims, citations</h3>
<p><b>Used:</b> <code>trait</code>/<code>object</code> dispatch (<code>Parents</code>, <code>Chain</code>), <code>extends CommutativeMonoidReduction[\V\]</code> + <code>Comprehension</code>, user <code>opr SUM()</code> (parsed as <code>BIG +</code>: <code>Parameter.rats:129</code>), <code>import FortressLibrary.{...} except { opr BIG + }</code> — the key discovery — generators <code>0#n</code>/<code>sequential</code>, <code>BIG MAXNUM</code>, <code>opr DOT</code>, juxtaposition overloads on <code>(V,V)</code> and <code>(Mat,Vec)</code>, mixed <code>RR64</code> overloads, <code>opr[i]</code>/<code>opr[i,j]</code>, tuple returns; correctly notes a parameterless <code>object</code> is a singleton (hence <code>Walk(seed)</code>). <b>Not used:</b> <code>excludes</code>, algebraic library traits for the scalar (the <code>AdditiveGroup[\D\]</code> route was probed and abandoned because it loses the Σ surface), library <code>Vector</code>/<code>Matrix</code> (rejected with two probes: bound unenforced but library <code>SUM</code> casts to <code>Number</code>), static <code>nat</code> dimensions.</p>
<p><b>Citations, all checked at the cited lines and accurate:</b> <code>reductions.tex:23-52</code> ("no explicit relationship between BIG Op and Op"); <code>traits.tex:231-239</code> (comprises); <code>FortressLibrary.fsi:277</code> (<code>Number comprises { RR64 }</code>, no ellipsis → sealed), <code>:1459</code>, <code>:1820-1822</code>; <code>FortressLibrary.fss:3041-3045</code>, <code>:3144-3149</code>, <code>:1114-1121</code>, <code>:2189</code>, <code>:2497</code>; <code>Expression.rats:685-707</code>; <code>PreTypeCheckDesugaringVisitor.java:351-405</code>; <code>precedence.tex:45-51</code>. Astra claims no language-level impossibility; each departure is classified with a reproducer.</p>
<h4>Reviewer reproducers for the two "interpreter gap" claims</h4>
<div class="scroll"><pre>RvwIndexedPow.fss    paren: 4.0
  bare g[1]^2.0  → ProgramError: …RvwIndexedPow.fss:10:23-25:
